   1:Source/html/jsenv.c **** /*
   2:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  * PlutoBrowser — jsenv.c
   3:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  * Basic JavaScript support (muJS/ES5). See jsenv.h for the design contract.
   4:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *
   5:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  * muJS facts this file relies on:
   6:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *   - js_ploadstring compiles without executing and returns non-zero on a
   7:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *     SyntaxError instead of longjmp-ing (report hook gets the message).
   8:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *   - js_pcall runs the loaded chunk with the error contained; the error
   9:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *     value is left on the stack top.
  10:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *   - js_setlimit(runlimit, memlimit): runlimit counts statements/back-edges
  11:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *     and throws a catchable "script ran too long"; memlimit caps each
  12:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *     individual allocation size (single-shot; "out of memory" thrown).
  13:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *   - Native functions registered with js_newcfunction + js_defglobal can
  14:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *     push their return values; js_pop(J, 1) in the wrapper discards them.
  15:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  *
  16:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  * document.write semantics: append-only capture. After all scripts run, the
  17:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  * CALLER feeds env result `output` back through document_parse and appends
  18:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  * the produced blocks (see document.c: doc_append_script_html).
  19:Source/html/jsenv.c ****  */
